WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.780
Okay, so last but not least for this introductory class from Real, we've got IES profiles.

2
00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:09.939
So we're going to take a look at what is an IES profile as well as how to set it up.

3
00:00:10.609 --> 00:00:15.650
So the Illuminating Engineering Society defined a file format which describes

4
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:23.839
the light distribution for a light source based on light source data from real-world measurements.

5
00:00:24.929 --> 00:00:32.530
The IES profile is a lighting industry standard which allows you to diagram the brightness and

6
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:36.929
the falloff of the light as it exists in a particular real-world light fixture.

7
00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:42.770
Now the cool thing is that we can grab this in Unreal and make it drive the light distribution

8
00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:47.810
of the light that we have. So how do we do this? It's really simple, we just go to the

9
00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:53.649
light profile section of the light in the details panel and assign one. So let's go ahead and do

10
00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:59.789
that real quick in the engine. So I'm going to bring in a spotlight here and you can see by default

11
00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:06.750
we just have a very basic shape on our light. I'm going to increase the intensity so we can

12
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:12.849
see it really really clearly. So you can see there, pretty standard light setup right. Now if

13
00:01:12.849 --> 00:01:18.780
I go to the profile section, if I scroll down, I've got an IES texture I can use. If I scroll

14
00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.299
down here I can use one of the ones that are pre-made here. So let's go ahead and look at

15
00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:27.739
Complex IES. So you can see that's now changed the way that this light is distributed.

16
00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:34.269
Let's take a look at it from a slightly more obvious point of view if we put it next to a wall

17
00:01:34.269 --> 00:01:47.629
like this where we can really see what the light is doing. So you can see very simple

18
00:01:47.629 --> 00:01:54.349
there and if we go back to that Complex IES you can see the change in the lighting distribution

19
00:01:54.349 --> 00:01:59.150
and that's down to that IES profile. I'm going to bring the intensity down so we can see a bit

